<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap wrap--narrow">
    <p class="eyebrow">Members · Edit</p>
    <h1>Edit draft</h1>
    <p class="lede measure">
      Everything about “<%= draft.title %>” except who reads it. The draft keeps its address,
      its discussion and its comments whatever you change here.
    </p>

    <%- include('../partials/form-errors', { errors: errors }) %>

    <form method="post" action="/drafts/<%= draft.id %>/edit" class="form card card--form" id="edit-form">
      <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>">

      <div class="field">
        <label for="title">Title</label>
        <input id="title" name="title" type="text" required maxlength="<%= limits.maxTitleChars %>"
               value="<%= values.title %>" placeholder="Chapter 4 — The long walk back">
      </div>

      <div class="field">
        <label for="description">What you'd like eyes on <span class="optional">(optional)</span></label>
        <textarea id="description" name="description" rows="3" maxlength="<%= limits.maxDescChars %>"
                  placeholder="Second draft. I'm unsure about the pacing after the argument."><%= values.description %></textarea>
      </div>

      <div class="field">
        <label for="author_name">Author name <span class="optional">(optional)</span></label>
        <input id="author_name" name="author_name" type="text" maxlength="<%= limits.maxAuthorChars %>"
               value="<%= values.authorName %>" placeholder="A pen name, or your co-author's name">
        <p class="hint">
          Leave blank to use your display name — or credit a pen name.
        </p>
      </div>

      <%# ------------------------------------------------------------------
          THE DISCUSSION TOPIC is threads.title for the thread this draft owns
          — the heading on /board and on /board/<id>. Upload set it to the
          draft's title, and blank still means exactly that, so a member who
          empties the field gets the default back rather than a nameless
          thread. Hidden entirely when a leader has removed the thread, the
          same condition views/drafts/show.ejs hides the conversation on.
          ------------------------------------------------------------------ %>
      <% if (hasThread) { %>
        <div class="field">
          <label for="topic">Discussion topic <span class="optional">(optional)</span></label>
          <input id="topic" name="topic" type="text" maxlength="<%= limits.maxTopicChars %>"
                 value="<%= values.topic %>" placeholder="<%= topicPlaceholder %>">
          <p class="hint">
            The heading this draft's conversation carries on the board. Leave it blank to go back
            to the draft's own title.
          </p>
        </div>
      <% } else { %>
        <p class="notice">
          This draft's discussion thread was removed by a leader, so there is no topic to name.
        </p>
      <% } %>

      <div class="form-actions">
        <button type="submit" class="btn btn--primary">Save</button>
        <a class="btn btn--sm" href="/drafts/<%= draft.id %>">Back to the draft</a>
      </div>
    </form>

    <%# ------------------------------------------------------------------
        REPLACING THE FILE is a separate form because it is a separate act:
        a full re-ingest that throws away every converted page and builds new
        ones. Same file rules as the upload page, and the kind may change —
        a Word draft can come back as a PDF.
        ------------------------------------------------------------------ %>
    <p class="form-legend">Replace the file</p>

    <p class="measure">
      The draft is converted again from scratch. It keeps its title, its byline, its address
      and its conversation — and it may change kind: swap a PDF in over a Word file and the
      reader simply becomes a PDF reader.
    </p>

    <p class="notice">
      <strong>Page comments stay put by page number.</strong> A note left on page 4 is still on
      page 4 of the new file, so if the replacement paginates differently those notes may sit
      against different words than they were written about. Nothing is deleted; nothing is
      re-anchored.
    </p>

    <noscript>
      <p class="notice">
        Replacing a file needs JavaScript switched on — the form sends the file straight to the
        server rather than reloading the page.
      </p>
    </noscript>

    <form method="post" action="/drafts/<%= draft.id %>/file" enctype="multipart/form-data"
          class="form card card--form upload-form" id="swap-form" data-csrf="<%= csrfToken %>">
      <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>">

      <p class="draft-meta">
        <span class="badge badge--kind"><%= kindLabel %></span>
        <span class="draft-by">· <%= draft.original_filename || 'the file on record' %></span>
      </p>

      <p class="form-legend">What are you uploading?</p>

      <div class="mode-switch" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Replacement type">
        <label class="mode-option">
          <input type="radio" name="mode" value="document" <%= values.mode !== 'images' ? 'checked' : '' %>>
          <span class="mode-body">
            <span class="mode-name">A document</span>
            <span class="mode-note">.docx, .pdf, .txt or .md — up to <%= limits.maxDocMb %> MB</span>
          </span>
        </label>
        <label class="mode-option">
          <input type="radio" name="mode" value="images" <%= values.mode === 'images' ? 'checked' : '' %>>
          <span class="mode-body">
            <span class="mode-name">A page sequence</span>
            <span class="mode-note">Graphic novels — up to <%= limits.maxImages %> images</span>
          </span>
        </label>
      </div>

      <div class="field mode-panel" data-mode-panel="document">
        <label for="document">Document file</label>
        <input id="document" name="document" type="file"
               accept=".docx,.pdf,.txt,.md,.markdown,application/pdf,text/plain,text/markdown,application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.wordprocessingml.document">
        <p class="hint">
          Word files keep their headings, so the reader gets a section menu. PDFs are shown
          exactly as laid out. Plain text and Markdown are split into ~1,000-word pages.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="field mode-panel" data-mode-panel="images" hidden>
        <label for="images">Page images</label>
        <input id="images" name="images" type="file" multiple
               accept=".jpg,.jpeg,.png,.webp,image/jpeg,image/png,image/webp" disabled>
        <p class="hint">
          JPG, PNG or WebP. Pages are ordered by filename, so name them
          <span class="mono">01.png</span>, <span class="mono">02.png</span>…
          Up to <%= limits.maxImages %> images, <%= limits.maxImageMb %> MB each,
          <%= limits.maxImagesTotalMb %> MB in total.
        </p>
        <ul class="file-list" data-file-list hidden></ul>
      </div>

      <div class="upload-progress" data-progress hidden>
        <div class="upload-bar"><span data-progress-bar></span></div>
        <p class="hint mono" data-progress-label>Uploading…</p>
      </div>

      <div class="form-actions">
        <button type="submit" class="btn btn--primary" data-submit>Replace the file</button>
      </div>

      <p class="form-aside">
        The draft's previous pages stay exactly where they are until the new ones are built.
        If the replacement will not convert, nothing is lost.
      </p>
    </form>
  </div>
</section>
